skill: voice-builder
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for the voice-builder skill. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-good-samples, Build my voice. Here are 6 of my best LinkedIn posts: [samples]., "reads brand-profile first if available|analyzes across the six layers (lexicon, syntax, rhetoric, structure, stance, negative space)|cites evidence (quotes from the samples) for the patterns it names|distills a 5-7 signature fingerprint plus a 'never' list|writes a voice.md following the template (operational rules, not adjectives)|runs the voice test: generates a post on a NEW topic and scores it against the fingerprint|shows the user the test post and what it changed"
  - no-samples-route-to-interview, Build my voice., "does NOT fabricate a voice from nothing|asks for samples, suggesting the easiest sources (incl. a spoken transcript/voice memo)|offers to fall back to brand-profile's voice interview if no samples exist|does not produce a confident voice.md without evidence"
  - thin-samples-low-confidence, Here's one short post I wrote. Build my voice from this., extracts what is observable from the limited sample|marks the voice.md confidence as low and names which layers are uncertain|asks for more samples (especially a spoken transcript) to raise confidence|does not overstate certainty
  - inconsistent-samples-voice-drift, "Here are my samples — some formal newsletters and some loose, funny tweets.", "does NOT average the conflicting samples into a bland middle|flags the inconsistency explicitly|asks which represents the target voice, or captures the split as channel-based tone variation|anchors the fingerprint on the target voice"
  - aspirational-voice, "I write pretty dry corporate stuff now, but I want to sound bold and punchy like [creator].", "separates current voice from target voice|collects or analyzes aspirational references and labels them as aspirational|is transparent about what is being borrowed vs. native|produces a target voice.md that is still ownable, not an impersonation"
  - multiple-voices-no-blend, Set up voice for our brand account and separately for our founder's personal account., "creates a separate voice.md per voice, clearly named|never blends the two voices together|notes anything genuinely shared vs distinct"
  - validation-loop-enforced, "Here are my samples — just give me the voice.md, skip the testing.", still runs at least one generate-and-score validation pass|explains briefly why an untested voice guide is unreliable|delivers the voice.md only after showing it can produce an on-voice post
  - exclude-bad-samples, Here are some samples — a couple are our legal/boilerplate website copy and one was written by an agency., "excludes ghostwritten, boilerplate, and committee-edited samples|explains why those don't represent the person's voice|builds the voice only from genuine first-person samples"
